<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8128" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνεκάς</span></b> , Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>upwards,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅταν . . μοῖρα πέμπῃ ἀ. ὄλβον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					2.22
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσπίδα φέρειν . . ἀ. ἐς τὸν οὐρανόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>V.</u>
					18
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				188
			</span></i>; [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρέπειν] τὸν αὐχέν᾽ ἐκ γῆς ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Crates Com.
					10
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. δ᾽ ἐπήρω τὸ σκέλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eup.
					50
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pherecr.
				169
			</span></i> (Valck.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς τὸ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Mul.</u>
					1.1
				</span></i>
			. (<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Thes.</u>
				33
			</span></i> wrongly derives the name of the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄνακες</span> from this word, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ
				γὰρ ἄνω τοὺς Ἀττικοὺς</span></div>
